  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "I can't tell which charge you mean from the earlier conversation, so I need you to confirm two things. Your account shows two card payments to **TechMart Online**, both settled:\n\n- **TX-0402**: EUR 240.00 on 14 July 2026\n- **TX-0401**: EUR 240.00 on 20 July 2026\n\nThe matching amounts and merchant could suggest a duplicate charge, but that's only a guess from the list.\n\nPlease tell me:\n1. **Which transaction** you want to dispute (TX-0401, TX-0402, or another).\n2. **What happened**, for example:\n   - You were charged twice for the same purchase (duplicate charge).\n   - You didn't make the payment (unauthorised debit or card-not-present fraud).\n   - You paid but didn't receive the goods (goods not received).\n   - You paid for a service that wasn't delivered (service not rendered).\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll run an eligibility check. I won't open a dispute unless that check passes, and I won't open one without your confirmation. If the check refuses it, I'll tell you why and suggest the next step.",
